[ RAND: THE RANDOM LINES OF FJCC68 FIG. 12, "ABOUT 1,000 STRAIGHT LINES
[ OF RANDOM LENGTH AND POSITION", FREELY TURNED BY THE DIALS.  THE
[ PICTURE HOLDS 4,000; NLINES SAYS HOW MANY ARE DRAWN.
[ SHOW IT WITH:   DSPLY (V.RAND, 2, , BUMP)!   CLOCK (DIALS+1, DI.EX)!
[ MORE OR FEWER:  OPEN (NLINES)!  THEN A NUMBER AND RETURN.  A NUMBER
[ ENDING IN A PERIOD IS DECIMAL: 2000. FOR 2,000 LINES.  WHEN THEY NO
[ LONGER FIT IN A FRAME, BUMP RAISES RATE AND TYPES IT (DSPLY P. 8).
V.RAND: TEXT /V.RAND/
        JSR (RANDN)
        RXYZ'IRL (DIALZ'DIR, DIALX'DIR, DIALY'DIR)
        IMG (RAND)
        RET
[ RANDN: CALLED BY THE JSR ITEM ABOVE, ONCE A FRAME.  IT ENDS RAND AFTER
[ NLINES LINES BY STORING A RET OVER THE NEXT DRAW'S COMMAND WORD, AND
[ PUTS BACK THE WORD IT TOOK THE LAST TIME.  NLINES IS KEPT FROM 1 TO
[ 4000.  EACH DRAW IS TWO WORDS; THE FIRST IS AT RAND.D.
RANDN:  0                       [ THE RETURN ADDRESS GOES HERE
        MDAR NLINES
        MDAE'F'N 1
        JPAN RN.LO              [ FEWER THAN 1
        MDAR NLINES
        MDAE'F'N 4000.
        JPAN RN.OK              [ FEWER THAN 4000
        MDAR'F 4000.
        JUMP RN.SET
RN.LO:  MDAR'F 1
        JUMP RN.SET
RN.OK:  MDAR NLINES
RN.SET: ARMD RN.C               [ THE COUNT TO SHOW
        MDXO RN.N
        JPLS RN.MV              [ NOT THE ONE SHOWN: MOVE THE END
        JUMP'I RANDN
RN.MV:  MDAR RN.SV
        ARMD'I RN.P             [ PUT BACK THE WORD THE RET TOOK
        MDAR RN.C
        ARMD RN.N
        MDAS RN.C               [ TWO WORDS A LINE
        MDAS'F RAND.D
        ARMD RN.P               [ WHERE THE NEXT DRAW STARTS
        MDAR'I RN.P
        ARMD RN.SV              [ KEEP ITS COMMAND WORD
        MDAR RN.RET
        ARMD'I RN.P             [ AND END THE PICTURE THERE
        JUMP'I RANDN
RN.C:   0
RN.N:   4000.                   [ AT START THE RET FOLLOWS ALL 4,000
RN.P:   RAND.D+8000.
RN.SV:  RET
RN.RET: RET
